# Line endings, made explicit so they don't depend on each machine's
# core.autocrlf: text files are stored LF in the repository (they already
# are) and checked out with the platform's native endings — CRLF on Windows.
#
# Declaring this also stops Windows working trees from reporting every file
# as modified-with-an-empty-diff when a tool rewrites files wholesale (e.g.
# a repo-wide `bun run fmt`), which is what prompted adding this file.
* text=auto

# Tool-managed files that are always written LF; keep them LF on disk too so
# the tools don't fight the checkout.
bun.lock text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never transform.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
